1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,749
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:06,749 --> 00:00:10,332
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:10,332 --> 00:00:13,161
Viewer discretion is advised.

4
00:00:13,338 --> 00:00:14,677
My name is Cheewa.

5
00:00:14,913 --> 00:00:16,198
You should hurry home, Glasses.

6
00:00:16,198 --> 00:00:17,425
Or you’ll get your money taken again.

7
00:00:17,425 --> 00:00:19,672
Can you walk me out?

8
00:00:19,889 --> 00:00:21,643
Astronomy Club.

9
00:00:21,643 --> 00:00:23,132
I’ve been waiting for you.

10
00:00:23,132 --> 00:00:25,560
But I don’t even know any of the planets you’re into.

11
00:00:25,698 --> 00:00:28,776
Once you learn more about something,
you’ll feel even closer to it.

12
00:00:28,776 --> 00:00:30,501
I’m not just into planets.

13
00:00:30,659 --> 00:00:32,261
I’m into you too.

14
00:00:32,261 --> 00:00:33,572
Can I hit on you?

15
00:01:38,549 --> 00:01:39,988
Asking if he could hit on me?

16
00:01:40,618 --> 00:01:41,785
What was he thinking?

17
00:01:47,236 --> 00:01:48,553
Can I hit on you?

18
00:01:49,715 --> 00:01:50,778
Hold on.

19
00:01:50,778 --> 00:01:51,365
I’m a bit dizzy.

20
00:01:51,365 --> 00:01:52,498
It felt like the world stopped turning
for a second.

21
00:01:52,675 --> 00:01:54,331
The world can’t stop spinning, P’Niran.

22
00:01:54,528 --> 00:01:58,064
The Earth spins at 1,675 kilometers per hour.

23
00:01:58,064 --> 00:01:59,841
If it stopped spinning for even one second,

24
00:02:00,156 --> 00:02:01,511
humans would all die.

25
00:02:01,511 --> 00:02:02,266
What are you talking about?

26
00:02:02,266 --> 00:02:03,194
Forget about humans!

27
00:02:03,194 --> 00:02:03,835
No.

28
00:02:03,835 --> 00:02:04,335
Huh?

29
00:02:04,552 --> 00:02:05,769
That means I’d die

30
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:07,581
and you would too.

31
00:02:07,857 --> 00:02:09,692
I can’t let that happen

32
00:02:11,130 --> 00:02:12,628
because you and I

33
00:02:16,232 --> 00:02:17,591
need to get together first.

34
00:02:20,289 --> 00:02:21,675
Or at least,

35
00:02:22,266 --> 00:02:24,645
become stars that shine side by side.

36
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,641
How’s he gonna hit on me?

37
00:02:37,094 --> 00:02:38,535
Who’s hitting on who?

38
00:02:38,535 --> 00:02:40,911
Damn. 7 a.m. sharp.

39
00:02:41,837 --> 00:02:44,068
Is this the first time
you’ve ever been early to school?

40
00:02:44,679 --> 00:02:45,582
What’s gotten into you?

41
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:46,348
Stop being dramatic.

42
00:02:46,663 --> 00:02:47,875
I’ve shown up around this time before.

43
00:02:47,875 --> 00:02:49,138
But what are you doing here?

44
00:02:49,492 --> 00:02:50,930
In my club?

45
00:02:50,930 --> 00:02:52,126
Does this club belong to you two?

46
00:02:52,323 --> 00:02:53,146
Seriously?

47
00:02:53,146 --> 00:02:56,902
Do you see anyone else using this room
besides the two of us?

48
00:02:57,296 --> 00:02:58,099
Me.

49
00:03:01,053 --> 00:03:03,582
Is something going on?

50
00:03:05,098 --> 00:03:05,882
Are you okay?

51
00:03:07,654 --> 00:03:08,474
Well…

52
00:03:10,404 --> 00:03:11,170
Nothing.

53
00:03:11,446 --> 00:03:13,598
Are you still worried about Auntie Tang?

54
00:03:13,716 --> 00:03:15,828
I already set the record straight in the chat.

55
00:03:16,005 --> 00:03:17,375
It’s a baseless rumor.

56
00:03:17,375 --> 00:03:18,491
People will forget about it soon.

57
00:03:19,042 --> 00:03:20,111
But what if they don’t?

58
00:03:23,656 --> 00:03:24,585
How about this?

59
00:03:25,235 --> 00:03:28,827
Let’s come up with a plan
to win those customers back for her.

60
00:03:29,418 --> 00:03:30,097
How?

61
00:03:30,097 --> 00:03:32,311
We play music to draw attention.

62
00:03:32,685 --> 00:03:34,923
You have Pok and me.

63
00:03:35,612 --> 00:03:36,501
Did you even ask me first?

64
00:03:39,691 --> 00:03:41,034
Make yourself at home.

65
00:03:41,034 --> 00:03:42,000
It’s my room.

66
00:03:43,135 --> 00:03:43,646
Thanks.

67
00:03:51,334 --> 00:03:52,258
Ugh.

68
00:03:52,376 --> 00:03:53,214
I think that’s a great idea.

69
00:03:53,214 --> 00:03:55,723
These two can sing and play guitar.

70
00:03:57,357 --> 00:03:58,467
It’s just singing.

71
00:03:58,467 --> 00:03:59,798
How would that make people buy her food?

72
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,017
Would it make them hungrier?

73
00:04:01,982 --> 00:04:02,791
I know what to do.

74
00:04:02,791 --> 00:04:03,625
Let’s give out free hugs.

75
00:04:03,625 --> 00:04:04,220
Free hugs?

76
00:04:04,574 --> 00:04:06,272
We give out free hugs.

77
00:04:06,902 --> 00:04:07,619
What are you doing?

78
00:04:08,170 --> 00:04:09,084
Be serious.

79
00:04:09,084 --> 00:04:10,229
I’m just trying it out.

80
00:04:10,879 --> 00:04:12,738
Whoever gets food from your auntie

81
00:04:12,915 --> 00:04:14,023
gets a free hug.

82
00:04:17,450 --> 00:04:18,676
But who will give out the hugs?

83
00:04:18,952 --> 00:04:19,625
You?

84
00:04:21,772 --> 00:04:22,449
Or you?

85
00:04:23,355 --> 00:04:24,426
Definitely you.

86
00:04:24,859 --> 00:04:26,406
You’re Auntie Tang’s nephew.

87
00:04:26,406 --> 00:04:28,606
Besides, you’re a national team athlete.

88
00:04:28,783 --> 00:04:29,911
Everyone knows you.

89
00:04:33,436 --> 00:04:35,156
Come on. Just give it a try.

90
00:04:35,550 --> 00:04:37,962
You have a tryout tomorrow anyway.

91
00:04:38,356 --> 00:04:40,119
You could get yourself some supporters too.

92
00:04:43,723 --> 00:04:45,837
What if no one comes for the food
or the hug?

93
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:47,524
I’d be so embarrassed.

94
00:04:49,021 --> 00:04:51,501
You’re P’Niran from the Judo Club.

95
00:04:51,757 --> 00:04:52,405
What are you afraid of?

96
00:04:52,661 --> 00:04:54,279
I’d be more worried about
the canteen going crazy.

97
00:04:56,485 --> 00:04:58,577
Let’s all give out hugs then.

98
00:04:58,853 --> 00:05:00,572
Give the customers options, you know?

99
00:05:03,289 --> 00:05:04,597
I think he’s the happiest about this idea.

100
00:05:05,109 --> 00:05:05,765
He wants to do it.

101
00:05:06,750 --> 00:05:08,383
Mr. Hot Stuff. Mr. Handsome.

102
00:05:09,624 --> 00:05:11,681
What are the seniors
from the Music Club doing?

103
00:05:11,878 --> 00:05:14,568
There are seniors from the Judo Club too.

104
00:05:14,568 --> 00:05:16,264
You can tell them about the free hugs now.

105
00:05:16,264 --> 00:05:18,915
Are those two clubs having a battle?

106
00:05:19,841 --> 00:05:21,547
The Judo Club fights with music.

107
00:05:22,354 --> 00:05:23,115
Go ahead.

108
00:05:24,513 --> 00:05:26,172
Go. Let’s do this.

109
00:05:42,766 --> 00:05:43,718
Hi, everyone.

110
00:05:44,171 --> 00:05:45,420
I’m Niran.

111
00:05:45,893 --> 00:05:48,214
I brought my friends to play some music.

112
00:05:49,356 --> 00:05:50,675
I hope you all like it.

113
00:05:52,191 --> 00:05:54,920
Actually, I have something to tell you.

114
00:05:57,027 --> 00:05:59,788
The rumor about Auntie Tang’s
isn’t true.

115
00:06:00,556 --> 00:06:03,580
Her food stall
is clean and safe.

116
00:06:03,954 --> 00:06:05,520
She uses fresh ingredients every day.

117
00:06:05,737 --> 00:06:08,357
Most importantly, her food tastes really good.

118
00:06:09,184 --> 00:06:10,564
As you all know,

119
00:06:11,056 --> 00:06:13,359
someone made up that rumor.

120
00:06:13,359 --> 00:06:14,339
Oh, someone made up that rumor.

121
00:06:14,339 --> 00:06:15,448
But never mind.

122
00:06:16,118 --> 00:06:18,979
If any of you have enjoyed
Auntie Tang’s food before,

123
00:06:19,432 --> 00:06:21,782
come enjoy it again today.

124
00:06:22,196 --> 00:06:23,936
She’s waiting for you all with a sweet smile.

125
00:06:27,698 --> 00:06:28,857
Well…

126
00:06:30,945 --> 00:06:32,961
Today I have something to give out too.

127
00:06:34,024 --> 00:06:36,167
Whoever gets food from Auntie Tang today

128
00:06:38,629 --> 00:06:39,826
gets a free hug

129
00:06:39,826 --> 00:06:41,346
from me and…

130
00:06:42,094 --> 00:06:43,480
my friends here.

131
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,428
Any one of us.

132
00:06:45,866 --> 00:06:49,245
Just get food from Auntie Tang,
and I’ll get to hug you, P’Niran?

133
00:06:53,243 --> 00:06:53,961
That’s right.

134
00:07:02,429 --> 00:07:03,676
I’m here for a free hug.

135
00:07:04,444 --> 00:07:04,986
Huh?

136
00:07:05,892 --> 00:07:06,653
What did you say?

137
00:07:08,012 --> 00:07:10,548
I get my food from Auntie Tang every day.

138
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:13,802
Only from her stall.

139
00:07:17,603 --> 00:07:19,066
So let’s hug now.

140
00:07:47,641 --> 00:07:52,439
(Is the world… coming to a stop?)

141
00:07:53,719 --> 00:07:57,710
(I guess all humans… are dying.)

142
00:07:59,719 --> 00:08:03,545
(Just like… this kid told me.)

143
00:08:15,738 --> 00:08:16,836
All done.

144
00:08:18,293 --> 00:08:20,463
Thank you for the gift from Auntie Tang’s.

145
00:08:22,334 --> 00:08:24,072
Today, her food tastes even better than ever.

146
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:35,515
And…

147
00:08:38,135 --> 00:08:39,691
when you hug other people,

148
00:08:41,463 --> 00:08:43,146
the world doesn’t have to stop spinning.

149
00:08:45,509 --> 00:08:47,130
Just hurry up and get the hug over with.

150
00:08:57,408 --> 00:08:58,693
Your food is over there.

151
00:09:00,446 --> 00:09:01,248
Thank you.

152
00:09:26,815 --> 00:09:28,338
Did you see Auntie Tang’s face?

153
00:09:28,338 --> 00:09:30,398
She looked so happy.

154
00:09:30,595 --> 00:09:32,412
The food sold out so quickly.

155
00:09:32,963 --> 00:09:34,900
The juniors were fighting each other to buy it.

156
00:09:35,668 --> 00:09:37,888
“I really want to hug P’Niran.”

157
00:09:38,065 --> 00:09:39,042
It’s so annoying.

158
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:41,006
Please. I got plenty of hugs too.

159
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,802
Same with Thara.

160
00:09:44,574 --> 00:09:45,750
Are you spacing out?

161
00:09:46,124 --> 00:09:47,903
All that hugging must've
turned your brain to mush.

162
00:09:47,903 --> 00:09:48,697
I’m not spacing out.

163
00:09:48,914 --> 00:09:50,019
I’m just tired.

164
00:09:50,787 --> 00:09:52,112
By the way,

165
00:09:52,112 --> 00:09:54,470
Cheewa was the first to ask Niran for a hug.

166
00:09:54,470 --> 00:09:55,064
Yeah.

167
00:09:55,478 --> 00:09:56,959
I thought he was going to shoo us away.

168
00:09:57,373 --> 00:09:59,653
Turns out he wanted a hug.

169
00:10:01,544 --> 00:10:02,623
Let’s put these things away.

170
00:10:12,458 --> 00:10:13,713
You okay today?

171
00:10:14,186 --> 00:10:14,907
Okay about what?

172
00:10:15,537 --> 00:10:16,832
About me hugging you.

173
00:10:19,431 --> 00:10:20,535
Of course, I was okay with it.

174
00:10:20,654 --> 00:10:22,426
My friends and I made that rule.

175
00:10:23,371 --> 00:10:24,260
What were you thinking, though?

176
00:10:24,555 --> 00:10:25,835
Why did you hug me?

177
00:10:25,835 --> 00:10:27,718
Just claiming what I was entitled to.

178
00:10:27,856 --> 00:10:29,617
You didn’t have to do that.
No one forced you to.

179
00:10:30,247 --> 00:10:32,677
You could’ve just lined up
to get food as usual.

180
00:10:35,021 --> 00:10:37,064
But according to your rule,

181
00:10:37,261 --> 00:10:39,615
I had to get in line for your hug anyway.

182
00:10:39,989 --> 00:10:41,368
I’d be at the front of the line too.

183
00:10:42,156 --> 00:10:44,719
Tell me honestly.

184
00:10:45,822 --> 00:10:47,669
Aren’t you shy at all?

185
00:10:48,831 --> 00:10:50,580
You just told me yesterday
you were hitting on me.

186
00:10:50,580 --> 00:10:52,560
Today, you already hugged me.

187
00:10:52,836 --> 00:10:54,166
I’m not shy at all.

188
00:10:55,978 --> 00:10:58,343
What’s wrong? Are you shy?

189
00:11:03,385 --> 00:11:06,245
Why is it so easy for you to say everything?

190
00:11:07,092 --> 00:11:08,422
Do you even have feelings?

191
00:11:09,072 --> 00:11:10,277
You act like a robot.

192
00:11:15,398 --> 00:11:17,040
Just because I’m not shy around you,

193
00:11:17,256 --> 00:11:18,606
I seem like a robot?

194
00:11:21,403 --> 00:11:22,833
It’s a mix of…

195
00:11:23,207 --> 00:11:24,805
many things.

196
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:26,392
It’s not just about being shy.

197
00:11:32,753 --> 00:11:36,084
If you don’t have bad feelings toward me
right now, and…

198
00:11:39,176 --> 00:11:41,689
maybe you’re feeling shy deep in there,

199
00:11:53,059 --> 00:11:54,915
that means I’m one step closer

200
00:11:59,228 --> 00:12:00,861
to winning you over, P’Niran.

201
00:12:10,626 --> 00:12:12,104
Are you the best in your school?

202
00:12:12,104 --> 00:12:13,793
I’ve thrown people bigger than you.

203
00:12:13,793 --> 00:12:15,408
It’s because you’re like this, Niran.

204
00:12:15,408 --> 00:12:16,741
You have a big ego.

205
00:12:16,741 --> 00:12:18,000
You’re too proud to lose.

206
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,135
But listen to me today.

207
00:12:31,106 --> 00:12:32,019
What are you talking about?

208
00:12:32,408 --> 00:12:33,679
If you want to make sure,

209
00:12:35,007 --> 00:12:37,608
you can try hugging me again now.

210
00:12:40,775 --> 00:12:41,571
Please.

211
00:12:46,499 --> 00:12:47,912
Are you testing me or something?

212
00:12:48,161 --> 00:12:49,488
Is there a camera somewhere?

213
00:12:49,488 --> 00:12:50,598
It’s not funny.

214
00:12:52,973 --> 00:12:54,316
I’m seriously hitting on you.

215
00:12:57,888 --> 00:12:58,428
Ugh!

216
00:12:59,292 --> 00:13:00,288
Fine.

217
00:13:00,288 --> 00:13:01,169
Just do whatever you want.

218
00:13:04,128 --> 00:13:04,958
Why are you smiling so much?

219
00:13:05,424 --> 00:13:07,208
Someday, you’ll smile at me like this.

220
00:13:11,162 --> 00:13:12,521
I saw the activity schedule.

221
00:13:13,267 --> 00:13:16,146
Tomorrow, you have a tryout
for a spot in the Athletes' Village, right?

222
00:13:19,902 --> 00:13:21,300
Mm, yeah.

223
00:13:22,005 --> 00:13:22,769
Why?

224
00:13:23,246 --> 00:13:24,252
Are you coming to watch me?

225
00:13:24,833 --> 00:13:26,934
I have a test tomorrow morning.

226
00:13:27,370 --> 00:13:28,557
I might not be able to make it,

227
00:13:29,242 --> 00:13:31,578
but I’m rooting for you, P’Niran.

228
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:35,792
Fine. Thanks.

229
00:13:37,078 --> 00:13:39,394
After the match, I have a reward for you.

230
00:13:40,016 --> 00:13:40,982
What reward?

231
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,666
Can’t you give it to me in advance?

232
00:13:42,848 --> 00:13:45,411
No. Wait until the match is over.

233
00:13:49,332 --> 00:13:50,910
What if I lose?

234
00:13:51,387 --> 00:13:52,726
Will I still get my reward?

235
00:13:54,905 --> 00:13:56,372
Try winning first.

236
00:13:58,468 --> 00:14:00,168
You got this, P’Niran.

237
00:14:02,450 --> 00:14:04,394
There’s nothing you can’t do.

238
00:14:05,784 --> 00:14:08,668
Even today, you put a smile back on
Auntie Tang’s face.

239
00:14:08,668 --> 00:14:09,705
And mine too.

240
00:14:13,274 --> 00:14:14,904
What’s with you, kid?

241
00:14:15,568 --> 00:14:16,754
Go home!

242
00:14:19,182 --> 00:14:20,203
Stop smiling already.

243
00:14:20,203 --> 00:14:20,934
Go!

244
00:14:24,503 --> 00:14:25,378
Are you coming or not?

245
00:14:32,101 --> 00:14:32,865
Hey.

246
00:14:32,865 --> 00:14:34,151
Everyone keeps saying

247
00:14:34,151 --> 00:14:37,544
Most is going to win a spot
in the Athletes’ Village.

248
00:14:39,183 --> 00:14:40,172
I mean, he’s really good.

249
00:14:40,172 --> 00:14:40,990
He deserves it.

250
00:14:40,990 --> 00:14:41,963
I could use a friend too.

251
00:14:44,391 --> 00:14:45,720
Jace is here today, right?

252
00:14:47,297 --> 00:14:48,506
We’re competing against his school.

253
00:14:49,813 --> 00:14:50,565
Yeah.

254
00:14:50,814 --> 00:14:52,449
You’re the one competing against him.

255
00:14:53,466 --> 00:14:55,003
That’s why Coach made you practice
so hard.

256
00:14:55,608 --> 00:14:57,064
Don’t underestimate Jace.

257
00:14:57,375 --> 00:14:58,721
He’s tough.

258
00:14:58,949 --> 00:15:01,905
I don’t think anyone from our school
could beat him except you.

259
00:15:07,608 --> 00:15:09,369
Are you the best in your school?

260
00:15:12,004 --> 00:15:13,173
Stop talking, Jace.

261
00:15:14,044 --> 00:15:16,126
I’ve thrown people bigger than you.

262
00:15:18,010 --> 00:15:18,678
Hmm.

263
00:15:24,711 --> 00:15:25,449
Bow!

264
00:16:09,079 --> 00:16:09,669
See?

265
00:16:10,728 --> 00:16:13,654
This is what happens
when you miss practice.

266
00:16:16,994 --> 00:16:18,105
I’m sorry, Coach.

267
00:16:21,237 --> 00:16:23,991
It's not just about missing out
on the Athletes' Village.

268
00:16:24,613 --> 00:16:27,924
You almost lost your spot
on the national team.

269
00:16:28,837 --> 00:16:29,793
I’m sorry, Coach.

270
00:16:30,747 --> 00:16:31,439
I’m sorry.

271
00:16:40,921 --> 00:16:41,646
Hey.

272
00:16:43,288 --> 00:16:44,403
I’m your teacher

273
00:16:44,652 --> 00:16:46,534
and your head coach, Niran.

274
00:16:47,343 --> 00:16:48,903
I’m not just anyone.

275
00:16:50,128 --> 00:16:51,696
Don’t let yourself get like this

276
00:16:52,443 --> 00:16:54,280
without anyone to turn to.

277
00:17:00,338 --> 00:17:04,492
I don’t know what’s on your mind right now.

278
00:17:05,031 --> 00:17:06,674
But just know one thing.

279
00:17:08,023 --> 00:17:11,037
I’m worried about you.

280
00:17:11,701 --> 00:17:12,961
And I’m always on your side.

281
00:17:19,351 --> 00:17:20,050
Okay.

282
00:17:36,719 --> 00:17:39,524
Yeah, he got beaten badly.

283
00:17:40,416 --> 00:17:43,485
I bet everyone from Jace’s school
was laughing their heads off.

284
00:17:43,608 --> 00:17:45,806
Niran must be frustrated.

285
00:17:46,387 --> 00:17:49,758
He should’ve gotten a spot
in the Athletes’ Village this year,

286
00:17:49,945 --> 00:17:51,808
but Most ended up getting it instead.

287
00:17:51,808 --> 00:17:53,204
It’s no surprise.

288
00:17:53,204 --> 00:17:54,768
Niran keeps skipping practice.

289
00:17:54,768 --> 00:17:56,784
Soon, his best friend Thara will surpass him.

290
00:17:56,784 --> 00:17:57,433
Trust me.

291
00:17:57,433 --> 00:17:58,941
Soon, you’ll be better than him.

292
00:18:18,803 --> 00:18:22,251
Hey, P’Niran lost.

293
00:18:22,251 --> 00:18:23,472
How could he lose?

294
00:18:24,384 --> 00:18:25,238
Really?

295
00:18:28,082 --> 00:18:29,707
But he’s always won.

296
00:18:31,331 --> 00:18:31,955
Ahem.

297
00:18:32,183 --> 00:18:34,495
How’s my little judo athlete?

298
00:18:34,661 --> 00:18:37,111
I heard you got beaten badly
by the other school.

299
00:18:37,277 --> 00:18:39,013
Leave me alone, Oy.

300
00:18:39,013 --> 00:18:40,642
Come on.

301
00:18:40,912 --> 00:18:42,720
You lost. Just admit it.

302
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:44,761
In sports, you win some and you lose some.

303
00:18:44,989 --> 00:18:46,278
Why are you making a fuss?

304
00:18:51,486 --> 00:18:53,190
It’s because you’re like this, Niran.

305
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:55,028
You have a big ego.

306
00:18:55,028 --> 00:18:56,203
You’re too proud to lose.

307
00:18:56,203 --> 00:18:58,391
Listen to me.

308
00:18:58,785 --> 00:19:01,727
You lost today. Your ranking dropped.

309
00:19:01,727 --> 00:19:03,701
Your ranking dropped.

310
00:19:06,323 --> 00:19:09,983
Loser.

311
00:19:09,983 --> 00:19:10,896
Let’s go.

312
00:19:11,041 --> 00:19:11,836
Where are we going?

313
00:19:13,608 --> 00:19:15,300
It’d be better if you came and helped me
with some work.

314
00:19:17,968 --> 00:19:20,853
Don’t stand here listening to
all this negativity.

315
00:19:22,513 --> 00:19:23,728
What, four-eyes?

316
00:19:24,890 --> 00:19:26,259
You just took him away like that?

317
00:19:27,448 --> 00:19:28,656
What’s wrong with him?

318
00:19:37,017 --> 00:19:40,073
So you really brought me here
to help you with work.

319
00:19:40,073 --> 00:19:40,728
Yes.

320
00:19:41,558 --> 00:19:44,052
I told you it’d be better
to come help me work.

321
00:19:47,608 --> 00:19:49,284
I thought you were going to comfort me.

322
00:19:51,794 --> 00:19:53,346
But you really brought me to work.

323
00:19:56,088 --> 00:19:58,207
Do you want me to comfort you, P’Niran?

324
00:19:58,608 --> 00:19:59,508
No.

325
00:20:00,815 --> 00:20:02,126
Just asking.

326
00:20:02,686 --> 00:20:04,187
You dragged me away.

327
00:20:04,187 --> 00:20:06,650
Why did you just stand there
and let them insult you?

328
00:20:07,608 --> 00:20:09,047
You didn’t say anything.

329
00:20:12,055 --> 00:20:15,090
I just wanted to hear what other people think.

330
00:20:15,463 --> 00:20:16,571
Why?

331
00:20:18,148 --> 00:20:19,141
Well…

332
00:20:20,199 --> 00:20:22,500
I don’t know.

333
00:20:23,226 --> 00:20:25,272
I just wanted to know
what people were saying about me.

334
00:20:25,272 --> 00:20:28,388
No one deserves to be insulted
just for losing a sports competition, P’Niran.

335
00:20:29,239 --> 00:20:30,951
You argue with everything I say.

336
00:20:32,984 --> 00:20:34,486
Why didn’t you talk back to the others too?

337
00:20:42,447 --> 00:20:43,770
I didn’t want to lose.

338
00:20:44,663 --> 00:20:46,242
I didn’t even want things to turn out this way.

339
00:20:48,483 --> 00:20:50,147
But I can't keep practicing
the way I have been.

340
00:20:51,184 --> 00:20:52,312
It’s too much for me.

341
00:20:53,868 --> 00:20:55,274
Why couldn't anyone understand me?

342
00:21:04,523 --> 00:21:07,042
Anyway, how did you know I lost?

343
00:21:07,332 --> 00:21:09,892
I thought you had a test
and couldn’t come watch.

344
00:21:33,345 --> 00:21:34,177
Full point!

345
00:21:34,841 --> 00:21:35,651
Match over!

346
00:21:38,514 --> 00:21:40,911
Are you sad that you lost?

347
00:21:50,261 --> 00:21:51,183
Of course I am.

348
00:21:55,519 --> 00:21:56,446
Why do you ask?

349
00:21:57,380 --> 00:21:58,281
Are you going to comfort me?

350
00:22:01,186 --> 00:22:02,332
I’m thinking about it.

351
00:22:07,468 --> 00:22:09,022
Okay. So how are you going to comfort me?

352
00:22:09,769 --> 00:22:10,605
Show me.

353
00:22:14,328 --> 00:22:15,555
Want a free hug?

354
00:22:16,115 --> 00:22:16,775
Huh?

355
00:22:18,414 --> 00:22:19,889
Just like at Auntie Tang’s.

356
00:22:21,653 --> 00:22:22,548
Are you crazy?

357
00:22:23,814 --> 00:22:25,282
I’m not hugging you again.

358
00:22:26,797 --> 00:22:28,455
Get back to work.

359
00:22:37,608 --> 00:22:38,905
What? Why are you smiling?

360
00:22:40,503 --> 00:22:41,650
Just keep working.

361
00:22:44,057 --> 00:22:46,415
If you’re exhausted,
can’t you just tell your coach?

362
00:22:53,713 --> 00:22:54,460
I can’t.

363
00:22:55,186 --> 00:22:57,210
Coach will call me lazy.

364
00:22:58,953 --> 00:23:01,520
He might have a good solution for you.

365
00:23:02,537 --> 00:23:05,276
He might be waiting for you to talk to him.

366
00:23:11,853 --> 00:23:13,413
Don’t keep it to yourself.

367
00:23:15,529 --> 00:23:17,597
You don't have to carry judo all by yourself.

368
00:23:18,946 --> 00:23:21,327
You've already taken on so much responsibility.

369
00:23:22,759 --> 00:23:25,073
Try giving the people around you a chance.

370
00:23:28,289 --> 00:23:31,070
Let them be a part of your life too.

371
00:23:39,794 --> 00:23:40,916
Fine.

372
00:23:41,621 --> 00:23:43,000
I’ll try talking to him.

373
00:23:44,203 --> 00:23:45,400
You nag so much.

374
00:23:48,325 --> 00:23:49,964
Why didn’t you press the elevator button?

375
00:23:49,964 --> 00:23:50,658
Ugh.

376
00:24:06,619 --> 00:24:07,679
Thanks, Glasses.

377
00:24:11,289 --> 00:24:14,020
Oh, I forgot

378
00:24:14,020 --> 00:24:15,189
Your name’s not Glasses.

379
00:24:20,334 --> 00:24:23,259
♪ What's going on? Something’s shaking ♪

380
00:24:23,259 --> 00:24:24,084
The elevator’s here.

381
00:24:24,084 --> 00:24:25,521
♪ Like the earth is moving ♪

382
00:24:25,521 --> 00:24:26,070
Okay.

383
00:24:26,070 --> 00:24:28,554
♪ Yesterday, there was nothing there ♪

384
00:24:28,554 --> 00:24:29,199
Get in.

385
00:24:29,780 --> 00:24:32,115
♪ Why today do I suddenly care? ♪

386
00:24:35,011 --> 00:24:38,472
So I told Coach directly that
I’m exhausted and need a break.

387
00:24:39,008 --> 00:24:39,815
Yeah.

388
00:24:40,064 --> 00:24:40,924
Damn.

389
00:24:41,069 --> 00:24:42,408
Didn’t he scold you?

390
00:24:43,113 --> 00:24:44,794
I was scared he would,

391
00:24:45,271 --> 00:24:46,558
but he didn’t.

392
00:24:46,890 --> 00:24:48,361
He said he understands.

393
00:24:48,608 --> 00:24:49,787
And he adjusted my schedule.

394
00:24:49,787 --> 00:24:50,726
Yeah.

395
00:24:52,158 --> 00:24:53,116
You’re brave.

396
00:24:53,718 --> 00:24:57,032
Who else in our club would dare
to ask for a schedule adjustment?

397
00:24:57,592 --> 00:24:58,385
No one.

398
00:24:58,924 --> 00:25:00,812
What do you mean by needing a break?

399
00:25:01,455 --> 00:25:02,579
I’m exhausted, Coach.

400
00:25:04,176 --> 00:25:06,187
I’m sorry I didn’t tell you directly, but…

401
00:25:08,552 --> 00:25:10,855
I’m more exhausted than I can handle.

402
00:25:13,033 --> 00:25:14,325
I’m stressed too.

403
00:25:17,209 --> 00:25:21,636
I don’t think I can enjoy judo like I used to.

404
00:25:27,652 --> 00:25:30,274
This is very normal, Niran.

405
00:25:31,125 --> 00:25:34,318
Almost every athlete
goes through this feeling.

406
00:25:35,293 --> 00:25:38,606
I’ll lighten your training schedule.

407
00:25:39,768 --> 00:25:41,179
Would that be okay?

408
00:25:43,254 --> 00:25:44,217
Honestly,

409
00:25:44,424 --> 00:25:46,796
if Cheewa hadn’t encouraged me,
I wouldn’t have dared.

410
00:25:46,796 --> 00:25:49,344
But you’re not quitting, are you?

411
00:25:49,904 --> 00:25:51,210
If you’re going to make that kind of decision,

412
00:25:51,667 --> 00:25:53,115
you have to tell me first.

413
00:25:57,132 --> 00:25:58,490
- Hi.
- Hello.

414
00:25:58,594 --> 00:25:59,850
Are you here for the lecture?

415
00:25:59,850 --> 00:26:01,163
Wanna play basketball with me?

416
00:26:03,899 --> 00:26:06,253
P’Niran and I live seven houses apart.

417
00:26:17,610 --> 00:26:19,025
If you’re going to make that kind of decision,

418
00:26:19,437 --> 00:26:20,548
you have to tell me first.

419
00:26:21,832 --> 00:26:24,017
No, I’m not quitting.

420
00:26:25,136 --> 00:26:27,422
Judo is still my favorite hobby.

421
00:26:29,677 --> 00:26:31,810
By the way, he’s good.

422
00:26:32,485 --> 00:26:33,798
That Cheewa kid from Grade 11.

423
00:26:35,411 --> 00:26:37,549
At least, he’s good for you.

424
00:26:59,030 --> 00:27:02,474
Could you check pages 2 and 3?

425
00:27:03,281 --> 00:27:04,449
Teacher Boriboon, hello.

426
00:27:04,679 --> 00:27:06,279
Hi.

427
00:27:06,279 --> 00:27:07,373
Are you here for the lecture?

428
00:27:07,373 --> 00:27:09,654
Great. Grade 10 is in charge of that today.

429
00:27:09,654 --> 00:27:10,499
But wait.

430
00:27:10,729 --> 00:27:11,897
Their class isn't over yet, right?

431
00:27:12,047 --> 00:27:13,322
Their teacher still hasn't let them out?

432
00:27:13,322 --> 00:27:13,822
Not yet.

433
00:27:13,822 --> 00:27:14,840
They’re not here yet.

434
00:27:15,007 --> 00:27:15,872
Oh, okay.

435
00:27:15,872 --> 00:27:17,261
Actually, I’m here for—

436
00:27:17,261 --> 00:27:18,325
You’re here for the lecture.

437
00:27:18,325 --> 00:27:21,724
Today, the 10th-graders are going to
talk about natural satellites.

438
00:27:21,724 --> 00:27:23,230
It’s actually very interesting, you know?

439
00:27:23,230 --> 00:27:23,730
Yeah.

440
00:27:23,730 --> 00:27:25,497
You girls should learn about that too.

441
00:27:51,176 --> 00:27:52,995
How did you know I'd go find you upstairs?

442
00:27:53,917 --> 00:27:56,490
I knew you’d probably want to tell me
about your conversation with your coach,

443
00:27:57,527 --> 00:27:59,203
so I left you a Post-it.

444
00:27:59,327 --> 00:27:59,827
Mm.

445
00:28:00,798 --> 00:28:02,838
He really adjusted my schedule.

446
00:28:03,447 --> 00:28:04,443
It wasn’t hard at all.

447
00:28:04,723 --> 00:28:05,721
All this time,

448
00:28:06,824 --> 00:28:08,127
everyone thought he was scary,

449
00:28:09,131 --> 00:28:10,125
so we were afraid to speak up.

450
00:28:13,449 --> 00:28:14,286
That’s great.

451
00:28:15,142 --> 00:28:16,379
Now you won’t be so exhausted.

452
00:28:16,955 --> 00:28:19,263
You’ll have time to rest and think about
what to do with the sport.

453
00:28:26,289 --> 00:28:27,608
Wanna play basketball with me?

454
00:28:29,369 --> 00:28:29,928
Who?

455
00:28:30,191 --> 00:28:30,882
Me?

456
00:28:31,277 --> 00:28:31,777
Yes.

457
00:28:32,254 --> 00:28:32,951
With you?

458
00:28:33,181 --> 00:28:33,933
With me.

459
00:28:35,365 --> 00:28:36,593
Do you even know how to play basketball?

460
00:28:36,922 --> 00:28:38,805
I'm decent, but I'm not that good.

461
00:28:42,854 --> 00:28:43,869
Oh, you have potential.

462
00:28:44,017 --> 00:28:45,289
I calculated it based on
the angle of incidence.

463
00:28:45,289 --> 00:28:46,097
Stop it.

464
00:28:46,541 --> 00:28:47,390
Just play basketball.

465
00:28:47,736 --> 00:28:49,346
Don’t say anything complicated again, okay?

466
00:28:49,346 --> 00:28:49,846
Okay.

467
00:28:51,656 --> 00:28:52,423
Give it back.

468
00:28:55,221 --> 00:28:56,604
Try and take it back yourself.

469
00:28:59,830 --> 00:29:00,673
Deal.

470
00:29:06,007 --> 00:29:06,667
Oh!

471
00:29:06,667 --> 00:29:09,492
Parncheewa, are you sure you’re not good?

472
00:29:14,655 --> 00:29:15,359
Hey!

473
00:29:19,424 --> 00:29:20,090
What?

474
00:29:21,667 --> 00:29:22,357
Be for real.

475
00:29:25,254 --> 00:29:26,636
How did you end up losing to me?

476
00:29:26,636 --> 00:29:27,590
Did you pretend to lose?

477
00:29:29,120 --> 00:29:31,925
I didn’t pretend. I really lost.

478
00:29:33,406 --> 00:29:35,695
You're better at the laws of motion than I am.

479
00:29:36,008 --> 00:29:37,036
- It’s only natural that you won.
- Stop it.

480
00:29:39,455 --> 00:29:40,351
No more explanations.

481
00:29:40,351 --> 00:29:40,932
I don’t get it.

482
00:29:41,245 --> 00:29:43,308
I just think you’re good at everything.

483
00:29:43,308 --> 00:29:44,793
How come you lost to me?

484
00:29:44,958 --> 00:29:47,026
I didn’t want to beat you.

485
00:29:47,750 --> 00:29:49,045
See? You pretended to lose to me.

486
00:29:49,539 --> 00:29:50,738
I didn’t.

487
00:29:51,660 --> 00:29:53,091
You’re lying. You pretended to lose.

488
00:29:53,256 --> 00:29:54,279
You’re accusing me.

489
00:29:54,839 --> 00:29:56,052
I could report you to the police.

490
00:29:56,908 --> 00:29:57,733
You’re just rambling.

491
00:29:59,774 --> 00:30:01,007
There’s one thing

492
00:30:02,571 --> 00:30:03,893
I want to win over, though.

493
00:30:10,381 --> 00:30:11,030
Why are you smiling?

494
00:30:13,762 --> 00:30:14,508
Stop it.

495
00:30:14,508 --> 00:30:15,808
I can guess what you’re going to say.

496
00:30:18,705 --> 00:30:19,980
I’m glad you know.

497
00:30:20,507 --> 00:30:21,431
That makes me happy.

498
00:30:27,047 --> 00:30:30,374
I might be pretending to know
when I actually don’t.

499
00:30:32,942 --> 00:30:33,566
What?

500
00:30:33,764 --> 00:30:34,525
Let’s do another match.

501
00:30:40,647 --> 00:30:41,389
Come on!

502
00:30:41,389 --> 00:30:43,190
Do you want to go singing after this?

503
00:30:44,655 --> 00:30:46,832
Beat me for real, and I’ll go.

504
00:30:47,704 --> 00:30:48,331
Deal?

505
00:30:50,240 --> 00:30:50,981
Yes.

506
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:51,734
Come on.

507
00:30:53,139 --> 00:30:53,832
I’ll start now.

508
00:30:59,080 --> 00:31:00,717
Hey!

509
00:31:01,359 --> 00:31:02,407
I can’t believe

510
00:31:02,621 --> 00:31:05,222
the Astronomy Club room has karaoke.

511
00:31:05,222 --> 00:31:07,214
It's for studious kids like us to unwind.

512
00:31:07,856 --> 00:31:09,189
We may look nerdy,

513
00:31:09,568 --> 00:31:11,769
but we all love screaming our heads off.

514
00:31:12,047 --> 00:31:13,888
That’s why Teacher Boriboon
set this up for us.

515
00:31:14,481 --> 00:31:15,215
That’s great.

516
00:31:15,462 --> 00:31:16,636
Come on. Who’s next?

517
00:31:16,636 --> 00:31:17,363
Go, Thara.

518
00:31:17,363 --> 00:31:17,863
It’s my turn.

519
00:31:18,571 --> 00:31:19,951
Cheewa, wanna sing with me?

520
00:31:21,235 --> 00:31:22,258
It’s okay.

521
00:31:22,472 --> 00:31:23,794
I’ll let you sing with your friends.

522
00:31:25,736 --> 00:31:26,906
Sing with me.
I’ve already chosen the song.

523
00:31:27,047 --> 00:31:28,048
Hey.

524
00:31:28,525 --> 00:31:30,361
If you’re going to let Niran sing,

525
00:31:30,937 --> 00:31:31,787
please just let me

526
00:31:31,932 --> 00:31:33,216
bang my head against a wall.

527
00:31:33,891 --> 00:31:37,153
Yeah, my friend here isn’t really good at
singing or dancing.

528
00:31:37,351 --> 00:31:38,095
Hey.

529
00:31:40,004 --> 00:31:42,228
If Niran is going to sing, let me know.

530
00:31:42,919 --> 00:31:43,541
Huh?

531
00:31:44,282 --> 00:31:45,287
You want to sing with him?

532
00:31:45,501 --> 00:31:46,899
I’m going to pack up and go home.

533
00:31:46,998 --> 00:31:49,141
Hey, my singing isn’t that bad.

534
00:31:49,437 --> 00:31:50,852
It's really that bad.

535
00:31:52,712 --> 00:31:53,321
Come on.

536
00:31:53,568 --> 00:31:55,202
Let P’Niran sing too.

537
00:31:55,317 --> 00:31:56,241
I want to hear it.

538
00:31:56,455 --> 00:31:57,194
Alright.

539
00:32:04,552 --> 00:32:05,306
Good job!

540
00:32:05,783 --> 00:32:07,619
Thanks for making the effort to clap for me.

541
00:32:07,619 --> 00:32:08,807
Thank god he stopped himself.

542
00:32:08,807 --> 00:32:10,574
Don’t be sad, P’Niran.

543
00:32:10,837 --> 00:32:12,885
Singing is something you can practice.

544
00:32:13,626 --> 00:32:18,283
Did you know it took aliens a really long time
to discover Earth?

545
00:32:20,291 --> 00:32:20,964
Huh?

546
00:32:21,079 --> 00:32:21,970
It’s true.

547
00:32:22,047 --> 00:32:24,395
They’re about 100 light-years away
from Earth.

548
00:32:24,872 --> 00:32:27,378
They saw Earth 100 years ago.

549
00:32:28,053 --> 00:32:29,007
Oh, come on.

550
00:32:29,205 --> 00:32:32,135
You always give such long explanations.

551
00:32:32,135 --> 00:32:33,306
Do you really think other people get it?

552
00:32:34,837 --> 00:32:38,607
Let’s just say I’m bad at singing
and need 100 years to practice.

553
00:32:39,397 --> 00:32:40,807
That’s how I take it.

554
00:32:41,054 --> 00:32:42,919
As for…

555
00:32:43,034 --> 00:32:44,191
your aliens,

556
00:32:44,191 --> 00:32:45,759
I’d rather not know about them right now.

557
00:32:47,047 --> 00:32:48,403
And you guys.

558
00:32:48,880 --> 00:32:49,596
Take that!

559
00:32:50,649 --> 00:32:51,845
Every single one of you.

560
00:32:53,050 --> 00:32:54,166
Has the storm calmed down?

561
00:32:54,528 --> 00:32:56,074
I was sitting here praying, all tense.

562
00:32:56,815 --> 00:32:57,517
Please.

563
00:32:57,632 --> 00:32:58,890
I was just singing, Hem.

564
00:32:59,894 --> 00:33:01,087
Don’t tease our friend.

565
00:33:01,729 --> 00:33:04,799
I thought someone was scraping their foot
against a sheet of metal just now.

566
00:33:04,799 --> 00:33:08,292
Please. There’s no one in this world
who sings that badly.

567
00:33:08,539 --> 00:33:09,344
There is.

568
00:33:09,607 --> 00:33:10,795
There really is.

569
00:33:11,206 --> 00:33:12,053
I’m not lying.

570
00:33:17,287 --> 00:33:18,908
Come hang out with us again next time.

571
00:33:19,237 --> 00:33:21,854
I mistook you for being too nerdy
to talk to normal people.

572
00:33:22,792 --> 00:33:24,384
I’m just a normal human.

573
00:33:24,828 --> 00:33:26,767
If you’re talking about aliens,

574
00:33:27,541 --> 00:33:29,561
did you know that
I have this one assumption?

575
00:33:29,561 --> 00:33:30,574
Stop.

576
00:33:31,529 --> 00:33:32,567
Save that for tomorrow.

577
00:33:32,567 --> 00:33:35,020
I really want to hear it, but I’m too exhausted.

578
00:33:35,020 --> 00:33:36,588
I’ll wait to hear about the aliens.

579
00:33:36,588 --> 00:33:37,261
I’m heading out.

580
00:33:37,261 --> 00:33:38,559
See you. Bye.

581
00:33:38,559 --> 00:33:39,257
You’re ditching us?

582
00:33:39,257 --> 00:33:39,769
Yeah.

583
00:33:40,082 --> 00:33:40,796
See you.

584
00:33:42,047 --> 00:33:43,313
Damn, he’s in a hurry to leave.

585
00:33:43,543 --> 00:33:44,156
Right?

586
00:33:44,617 --> 00:33:46,341
Oh, by the way,

587
00:33:46,703 --> 00:33:48,608
your house is on the same way as Niran’s?

588
00:33:49,047 --> 00:33:49,787
Yes.

589
00:33:50,116 --> 00:33:52,573
P’Niran and I live seven houses apart.

590
00:33:52,853 --> 00:33:53,592
Damn.

591
00:33:54,020 --> 00:33:54,860
What a coincidence.

592
00:33:56,061 --> 00:33:57,416
But why did you two never meet before?

593
00:33:57,646 --> 00:33:58,916
Because I leave early.

594
00:33:59,114 --> 00:34:00,421
P’Niran leaves late.

595
00:34:00,750 --> 00:34:01,429
Oh?

596
00:34:02,137 --> 00:34:02,784
Oh.

597
00:34:03,014 --> 00:34:04,455
Yeah, that makes sense.

598
00:34:04,455 --> 00:34:05,133
True.

599
00:34:05,133 --> 00:34:06,530
Learn to wake up early sometimes.

600
00:34:07,320 --> 00:34:09,332
Anyway, get home safe.

601
00:34:09,530 --> 00:34:10,687
We’re leaving now.

602
00:34:11,576 --> 00:34:12,295
See you.

603
00:34:13,217 --> 00:34:14,538
Bye, kids.

604
00:34:14,949 --> 00:34:16,732
Try to show up in time
for the morning assembly too.

605
00:34:16,732 --> 00:34:17,647
I still show up earlier than you.

606
00:34:18,865 --> 00:34:19,582
So?

607
00:34:21,787 --> 00:34:22,287
Let’s go home?

608
00:34:24,213 --> 00:34:25,170
Which way should we take today?

609
00:34:27,409 --> 00:34:28,400
Uh…

610
00:34:30,391 --> 00:34:32,004
Can you lead the way?

611
00:34:32,004 --> 00:34:32,631
What? No.

612
00:34:33,602 --> 00:34:34,399
You lead the way today.

613
00:34:34,399 --> 00:34:35,057
I’m always the one leading.

614
00:34:35,403 --> 00:34:36,669
Let’s go that way then.

615
00:34:36,669 --> 00:34:37,749
That gate is closed. Come this way.

616
00:34:40,407 --> 00:34:41,947
It looks like it’s going to rain.

617
00:34:42,047 --> 00:34:43,504
Once you’re inside,

618
00:34:43,504 --> 00:34:45,230
I’ll know for sure you won’t get soaked.

619
00:34:46,333 --> 00:34:49,963
You went from being the top rank in school
to where even are you now?

620
00:35:01,708 --> 00:35:04,509
That’s why Thipok thinks
it’s better to make his own music.

621
00:35:04,509 --> 00:35:06,779
But he sent his demos to a lot of labels.

622
00:35:07,640 --> 00:35:09,928
He’s just waiting to see if any of them
call him in.

623
00:35:11,244 --> 00:35:14,485
That explains
why P’Thipok has such a good voice.

624
00:35:15,265 --> 00:35:17,023
Actually, Hem is a good singer too.

625
00:35:17,023 --> 00:35:19,073
Everyone from the Music Club is.

626
00:35:19,659 --> 00:35:21,830
Meanwhile, I hang out there all the time,

627
00:35:22,050 --> 00:35:23,019
but I didn’t pick up a single thing.

628
00:35:23,019 --> 00:35:24,725
In one ear, out the other.

629
00:35:24,908 --> 00:35:26,533
Sometimes it comes out of my nose too.

630
00:35:31,384 --> 00:35:32,346
P’Niran.

631
00:35:34,726 --> 00:35:37,299
When we were in the karaoke room earlier,

632
00:35:38,269 --> 00:35:41,569
I didn’t mean
you need to practice singing for 100 years.

633
00:35:45,340 --> 00:35:46,248
Are you overthinking that?

634
00:35:48,152 --> 00:35:49,247
Don’t overthink it.

635
00:35:49,247 --> 00:35:50,198
I don’t even mind.

636
00:35:50,546 --> 00:35:54,508
I don’t want you to take it to heart
and lose your confidence.

637
00:35:56,705 --> 00:35:57,483
Cheewa,

638
00:35:58,087 --> 00:35:59,443
look at my friends.

639
00:35:59,846 --> 00:36:01,190
If I were going to get insecure,

640
00:36:01,465 --> 00:36:03,781
it’d be because of them, not aliens.

641
00:36:04,715 --> 00:36:05,319
Come on.

642
00:36:06,015 --> 00:36:07,021
You’re right.

643
00:36:07,552 --> 00:36:08,946
Your friends are way beyond aliens.

644
00:36:11,363 --> 00:36:12,325
I’m hungry.

645
00:36:13,735 --> 00:36:14,903
It’s not good to eat late at night.

646
00:36:15,818 --> 00:36:17,659
I’m just whining. I’m not actually going to eat.

647
00:36:18,593 --> 00:36:20,081
When you get to study with him, you’ll see.

648
00:36:20,081 --> 00:36:22,487
He keeps wearing black sunglasses
when he's actually sleeping.

649
00:36:22,835 --> 00:36:25,057
My friends and I tease him all the time.

650
00:36:29,048 --> 00:36:29,548
Hey.

651
00:36:30,225 --> 00:36:31,550
You should go home. It’s late.

652
00:36:32,319 --> 00:36:33,153
Hurry.

653
00:36:33,483 --> 00:36:34,552
The sky looks cloudy too.

654
00:36:34,735 --> 00:36:35,536
It’s definitely going to rain.

655
00:36:36,268 --> 00:36:36,938
Yes.

656
00:36:37,767 --> 00:36:38,404
Mm.

657
00:36:40,052 --> 00:36:41,907
Now start walking home.

658
00:36:42,786 --> 00:36:44,482
I’ll wait until you get inside.

659
00:36:44,885 --> 00:36:45,447
Why?

660
00:36:45,630 --> 00:36:46,624
My house is right here.

661
00:36:46,624 --> 00:36:47,757
I just have to step inside.

662
00:36:48,873 --> 00:36:50,563
Because it looks like it’s going to rain,

663
00:36:50,856 --> 00:36:52,556
just like you said.

664
00:36:53,709 --> 00:36:55,228
Once you’re inside,

665
00:36:55,869 --> 00:36:57,510
I’ll know for sure you won’t get soaked.

666
00:37:02,618 --> 00:37:03,853
Fine, I’m going in.

667
00:37:03,853 --> 00:37:05,127
You’d better hurry home.

668
00:37:08,364 --> 00:37:09,737
I know you’re watching me.

669
00:37:09,939 --> 00:37:11,120
Hurry home now, Glasses,

670
00:37:11,120 --> 00:37:11,802
or I’ll kick you.

671
00:37:15,830 --> 00:37:16,491
Go home.

672
00:37:29,183 --> 00:37:29,759
Hi, Dad.

673
00:37:29,759 --> 00:37:32,795
The school called to tell me
that your ranking dropped

674
00:37:33,582 --> 00:37:37,103
and you missed your chance
at the Athletes’ Village training.

675
00:37:41,002 --> 00:37:41,611
Yeah.

676
00:37:44,211 --> 00:37:45,817
How could you let this happen?

677
00:37:46,527 --> 00:37:47,273
Huh?

678
00:37:48,811 --> 00:37:50,259
Aren’t you embarrassed?

679
00:37:50,447 --> 00:37:52,368
You went from being the top rank in school

680
00:37:52,936 --> 00:37:54,940
to where even are you now?

681
00:37:55,361 --> 00:37:58,423
Well, the others are good too.

682
00:37:59,503 --> 00:38:02,145
If the others are good, just be better.

683
00:38:02,145 --> 00:38:03,709
If they train 10 days, you train 20.

684
00:38:04,148 --> 00:38:06,074
What’s so hard to understand?

685
00:38:09,571 --> 00:38:12,788
I’ll tell your coach to double down
on your training schedule.

686
00:38:13,337 --> 00:38:13,837
Alright?

687
00:38:14,990 --> 00:38:17,495
You’re not going anywhere over school break. You’ll practice every day.

688
00:38:18,960 --> 00:38:20,322
No wasting time on nonsense.

689
00:38:22,080 --> 00:38:23,088
I’m quitting judo.

690
00:38:27,866 --> 00:38:28,619
I’m quitting.

691
00:38:29,681 --> 00:38:30,839
I don’t want to do it anymore.

692
00:38:34,098 --> 00:38:35,587
What are you talking about?

693
00:38:35,587 --> 00:38:36,087
Huh?

694
00:38:37,076 --> 00:38:38,510
You’ve put so much into this.

695
00:38:38,510 --> 00:38:39,153
You can’t quit.

696
00:38:39,153 --> 00:38:40,605
How much is enough for me to quit?

697
00:38:40,769 --> 00:38:41,766
Just say it, Dad.

698
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:43,818
How much is enough?

699
00:38:44,514 --> 00:38:46,835
I can’t carry the weight of your expectations
anymore.

700
00:38:49,691 --> 00:38:51,277
Even if it’s just a sport,

701
00:38:52,412 --> 00:38:54,995
you’ve dedicated yourself to it for so long.

702
00:38:55,270 --> 00:38:56,327
Why are you being so rash?

703
00:38:56,327 --> 00:38:57,200
Rash?

704
00:38:57,749 --> 00:38:58,665
I’ve been thinking about this for a long time.

705
00:38:58,665 --> 00:38:59,727
It’s not a whim.

706
00:39:05,255 --> 00:39:06,650
You keep saying stuff like that.

707
00:39:07,675 --> 00:39:09,405
Have you ever really understood how I feel?

708
00:39:10,833 --> 00:39:13,062
Ah, I get it.

709
00:39:13,648 --> 00:39:17,243
Your friends do music.

710
00:39:17,554 --> 00:39:19,112
So you want to pivot.

711
00:39:20,447 --> 00:39:21,591
You want to be a singer.

712
00:39:21,902 --> 00:39:23,043
Make music.

713
00:39:24,014 --> 00:39:24,569
Right?

714
00:39:26,638 --> 00:39:27,381
Fair enough.

715
00:39:28,022 --> 00:39:29,220
Leave my friends alone.

716
00:39:31,143 --> 00:39:32,442
Then don’t lose.

717
00:39:33,339 --> 00:39:35,365
If you don’t lose, I’ll let you do anything.

718
00:39:37,452 --> 00:39:39,135
Yeah, I suck!

719
00:39:40,179 --> 00:39:41,514
I could never be like you!

720
00:39:44,242 --> 00:39:45,911
You don’t get this at all, Dad!

721
00:39:47,321 --> 00:39:48,646
Do you even understand anything?

722
00:39:51,520 --> 00:39:52,408
Screw it!

723
00:40:10,808 --> 00:40:11,593
What are you looking at?

724
00:40:14,167 --> 00:40:15,062
What are you looking at?

725
00:40:16,106 --> 00:40:17,316
There are no stars right now.

726
00:40:17,316 --> 00:40:19,270
Try looking up again, P’Niran.

727
00:40:26,831 --> 00:40:27,893
What are you even doing?

728
00:40:32,397 --> 00:40:33,380
There’s nothing up there.

729
00:40:33,929 --> 00:40:35,600
There’s nothing yet.

730
00:40:36,845 --> 00:40:39,025
But if you look up at the sky,

731
00:40:41,918 --> 00:40:44,790
your tears will flow back into your eyes.

732
00:40:49,605 --> 00:40:52,291
Or if you want to let them fall with gravity,

733
00:40:55,916 --> 00:40:57,395
then just cry it out.

734
00:41:13,770 --> 00:41:16,152
Why won’t you just go home?

735
00:41:19,777 --> 00:41:21,055
I’m just here

736
00:41:22,758 --> 00:41:25,125
in case you need someone at a time like this.

737
00:41:28,951 --> 00:41:30,758
Why do you think I need someone?

738
00:41:32,699 --> 00:41:35,447
I’m just here in case you do.

739
00:41:50,228 --> 00:41:51,307
You worry too much about me.

740
00:41:51,307 --> 00:41:51,991
You’re meddling.

741
00:41:53,968 --> 00:41:58,448
I don’t want to see you hurting alone
on a night like this.

742
00:42:00,810 --> 00:42:02,668
I’m staying here with you.

743
00:42:06,366 --> 00:42:07,337
P’Niran,

744
00:42:08,545 --> 00:42:09,879
I know it’s hard

745
00:42:10,245 --> 00:42:12,228
to deal with everything in there.

746
00:42:16,329 --> 00:42:18,127
But it’ll get better soon.

747
00:42:19,152 --> 00:42:21,302
You won’t feel like this forever.

748
00:42:23,060 --> 00:42:27,422
♪ Out of the blue, I don’t know what to do ♪

749
00:42:27,422 --> 00:42:30,830
♪ Out of the blue,
can’t get any words out to you ♪

750
00:42:30,830 --> 00:42:37,412
♪ Just one smile, and I’m blushing endlessly ♪

751
00:42:42,278 --> 00:42:43,916
What I was looking at just now…

752
00:42:45,545 --> 00:42:50,851
I was trying to see which star
would emerge from the dark clouds first.

753
00:42:55,807 --> 00:42:57,563
It’ll come out soon.

754
00:42:57,563 --> 00:42:58,440
In just a moment.

755
00:43:07,408 --> 00:43:08,114
Mm.

756
00:43:12,215 --> 00:43:14,934
I guess you won’t get to reward me, then.

757
00:43:15,959 --> 00:43:17,290
I lost.

758
00:43:21,556 --> 00:43:23,888
I was going to give you a gift anyway.

759
00:43:26,579 --> 00:43:27,783
Where is it? Give it to me.

760
00:43:33,445 --> 00:43:34,560
You get a free hug.

761
00:43:41,599 --> 00:43:43,778
This isn’t a prize for the winner.

762
00:43:45,170 --> 00:43:47,217
It’s a reward for being amazing.

763
00:43:50,036 --> 00:43:51,741
If you know you’re amazing,

764
00:43:54,267 --> 00:43:56,039
come and hug Cheewa.

765
00:43:56,204 --> 00:43:59,487
♪ Is this love I feel, am I calling it right? ♪

766
00:43:59,487 --> 00:44:02,515
♪ Is it why my heart beats faster tonight? ♪

767
00:44:03,207 --> 00:44:06,528
♪ I see you every day ♪

768
00:44:06,528 --> 00:44:08,802
♪ Yet I miss you again ♪

769
00:44:08,802 --> 00:44:10,204
I still want to look at the stars.

770
00:44:10,204 --> 00:44:12,077
Do you want to go to the planetarium with me?

771
00:44:12,187 --> 00:44:14,640
Ugh! Why do I have to wake up early?

772
00:44:14,767 --> 00:44:16,374
You really like this stuff, huh?

773
00:44:16,374 --> 00:44:17,408
You’re smiling like a kid.

774
00:44:17,408 --> 00:44:19,856
Can I be your little kid, P’Niran?

775
00:44:19,856 --> 00:44:22,488
Why is Parncheewa being so clingy with you?

776
00:44:22,488 --> 00:44:23,880
Just say you’re flirting with each other.

777
00:44:23,880 --> 00:44:24,990
Don’t say that to him.

778
00:44:24,990 --> 00:44:26,059
You’ll make him feel awkward.

779
00:44:26,059 --> 00:44:29,966
Are you uncomfortable with me
hitting on you?

780
00:44:30,327 --> 00:44:31,504
You’re down bad, Glasses.
